{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"hesitant-piny-spiketail","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# The typed no-region error names AWS_REGION as a fix, and it is not one — MEASURED\n\n## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.py` raises a typed `LLMConfigError` when no AWS region resolves, and its\nmessage instructs the operator to set \"a standard AWS region source (AWS_REGION / AWS_DEFAULT_REGION /\nthe active profile's config)\". The surrounding docstring says the same. **`AWS_REGION` alone does not\nwork**, so an operator who follows the error message exactly gets the identical error again, with\nnothing to indicate why.\n\nMEASURED in the production review-bot container (compose-review-bot-1 on i-00880b2c7f13527c5), on\n**botocore 1.43.62 / boto3 1.43.62** — a NEWER version than the 1.43.58 the original finding was made\nagainst, so this is not a stale observation:\n\n    AWS_DEFAULT_REGION genuinely UNSET (env -u), AWS_REGION=us-east-1\n      -> boto3.session.Session().region_name is None\n    both genuinely UNSET\n      -> boto3.session.Session().region_name is None\n    AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=us-east-1, AWS_REGION empty\n      -> boto3.session.Session().region_name == 'us-east-1'\n\nSo only `AWS_DEFAULT_REGION` (or a profile) resolves. This is exactly why\n`infra/compose/docker-compose.yml` sets BOTH `REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION` and `AWS_DEFAULT_REGION` for\nthe review-bot, and its inline comment already records the asymmetry correctly — the compose file is\nright and the module docstring/error message are wrong, so the two disagree in-tree.\n\nThe blast radius is operator time during an outage, on a path that is fail-closed by design: the\nBedrock provider refuses to construct without a region, so this message is precisely what a\nfirst-responder reads while the LLM-Review gate is not voting. Discovered while verifying the region\nstory for the production cutover [rebar:eb6e-f43a-e86b-443a].\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.py` — the `LLMConfigError` message and the module/function docstring\n  that both list `AWS_REGION` as a working source.\n\nNothing else: no behaviour change, no config change. The pre-check that produces the error is correct\nas written — it tests boto3's own resolution rather than inventing a default — and must not be altered.\n\n## Approach\n\nCorrect the text to name `AWS_DEFAULT_REGION` (and rebar's own `REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION`) as the\nsources that resolve, and state explicitly that `AWS_REGION` alone does NOT, with the botocore version\nthe claim was measured against so a future reader can tell whether to re-measure rather than assuming.\nDo not silently delete the `AWS_REGION` mention: an operator who has already set it needs to be told it\nis insufficient, which a bare omission does not do.\n\n## Testing\n\nA test asserting the error message does not offer `AWS_REGION` as a standalone remedy would be a\nchange-detector on prose. The oracle worth having instead is the behavioural one this ticket rests on:\nassert that with only `AWS_REGION` set, region resolution yields nothing and the typed\n`LLMConfigError` is still raised — so if a future botocore makes `AWS_REGION` work, the test goes GREEN\nin a way that flags the docstring as re-checkable rather than leaving it quietly wrong.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] the `LLMConfigError` message no longer presents `AWS_REGION` as a sufficient fix, and names\n      `AWS_DEFAULT_REGION` / `REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION` as the sources that do resolve.\n- [ ] the message or docstring states that `AWS_REGION` alone does not resolve, naming the botocore\n      version the behaviour was measured on, so the claim is falsifiable rather than folklore.\n- [ ] the module docstring and the error message agree with each other AND with the existing\n      `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml` review-bot comment, which already states the asymmetry\n      correctly — the in-tree contradiction is gone.\n- [ ] a test pins the BEHAVIOUR (only-`AWS_REGION` still fails to resolve and still raises the typed\n      error), not the prose, and is verified RED by mutating the pre-check away.","id":"4e71-f237-28c4-4c65","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"bedrock_model.py tells operators to set AWS_REGION, which does not resolve a region"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785796460697728001,"uuid":"e9f5e740-46be-40f3-94ca-9affec9a7a86"}